# rpg/art/doll/maps/stamps/boots_adult.stamps: the adult boot, ONE drawing in five tilts (docs/MOTION_P2.md 4 and 8; STYLE_P2
# 10 "The owner's motion reference"). Each key is a hand-placed rotation of A3's idle foot (the B rows F-2..F-1 and the Ink
# sole of legs/adult/loco/std's idle; the shaft above is the shin, drawn by the leg): never a shear, a squash or a tool
# rotation. K0 flat (the planted foot; 7 px sole); K1 toe-up (heel strike: the sole 3 px on the ground at the heel, then
# runs of 2 rising two rows to the toe; fix r2 R2-01: every K0 column lifted with the sole, so the toe cap keeps K0's two
# leather rows and its top runs parallel to the sole to a square tip: no notch, no lone toe pixel; fix r3 R3-03: the top
# outline carries back over the instep (`....fff`), so the shin's front edge closes into the top of the foot and no
# background notch opens between shin and toe cap (INSTEP 0); 22 px); K2 heel-off (fix
# r2: the same rotation about the toe, the heel two rows up, the ball's 3 px on the ground, K0's toe slope kept; sole runs
# 2,2,3, a runs-of-2 slope the gates class with K3's); K3 toe-off 1:2 (rolled onto the toe; runs of 2
# rising two rows; the swing foot toe down when lifted: every lifted or pointed foot since fix r3); K4 hang 1:1 (the run's
# kicked foot until fix r3; no longer placed: a 45 degree turn of this 20 px boot reads as a 2-row-deep stick). Every key
# keeps the square heel, the outline all round, the straight Ink sole, the heel's lit pixel and the toe's shade, within 1 px
# of K0's 20. `n` near, `f` far (a value darker, the same silhouette). origin = the key's ground pivot on its sole row (the
# heel of K0 / K1, the toe of K2 / K3 / K4). The L entries are the R keys mirrored and re-lit (outlines where the mirror
# puts them, the shading light-left again), never the plain mirror. Used by legs/adult/loco/std.pxm and tips.pxm (`put`,
# expanded there until pxc reads this library).
# (P2b motion proto2 i1, 2026-10-21) the far keys (K0f..K4f) are the idle's far value again (i2: two lit leather pixels
# then g; prototype i3's one flat dark read as an outline on grass, so the far leg looked thinner than it is).
use person
# K0 flat: A3's idle foot (B rows F-2..F-1, O sole F); origin = the heel on the sole row
stamp K0n R origin 0 2
|fhhhgf.
|fihhggf
|KKKKKKK
regions
|BBBBBB.
|BBBBBBB
|OOOOOOO
stamp K0f R origin 0 2
|fhhggf.
|fhhgggf
|KKKKKKK
regions
|BBBBBB.
|BBBBBBB
|OOOOOOO
# K1 toe-up (heel strike; sole runs 3,2,2 rising to the toe, the toe cap's top parallel to it, closed over the instep): origin = the heel
stamp K1n R origin 0 4
